    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q1">
    <h2>Q1 · Pure LFA singletons</h2>
    <p class="lede">Records whose <code>content_norm_sha256</code> appears on exactly one host in the fleet. This is the load-bearing query: an attacker who appends a malicious line to <code>/etc/crontab</code> on one host produces a digest no other host has, and it surfaces here.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q1">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q1">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>content_norm</th><th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th><th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        
          <tr>
            <td>cron</td><td>cron.d</td>
            <td class="hash">cron-singlet</td>
            <td>h1</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/cron.d/singleton-impl</td>
            <td class="snippet">cron-singleton-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td>cron</td><td>cron.daily</td>
            <td class="hash">sync-cron-no</td>
            <td>h5</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/cron.daily/sync</td>
            <td class="snippet">sync-cron-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td>profile</td><td>profile.d</td>
            <td class="hash">sync-profile</td>
            <td>h5</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/profile.d/sync.sh</td>
            <td class="snippet">sync-profile-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td>systemd</td><td>systemd.unit</td>
            <td class="hash">beacon-svc-n</td>
            <td>h4</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/systemd/system/beacon.service</td>
            <td class="snippet">beacon-svc-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td>systemd</td><td>systemd.unit</td>
            <td class="hash">sync-svc-nor</td>
            <td>h5</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/systemd/system/sync.service</td>
            <td class="snippet">sync-svc-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q2">
    <h2>Q2 · Per-locus LFA singletons</h2>
    <p class="lede">Like Q1 but also groups by <code>locus</code>. Catches the case where the same content is universal but appears at an unusual path on one host (renamed copy, look-alike location).</p>
