          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td>systemd</td><td>systemd.unit</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/systemd/system/sync.service</td>
            <td class="hash">sync-svc-nor</td>
            <td>h5</td>
            <td class="snippet">sync-svc-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q3">
    <h2>Q3 · Peer-group LFA by (os_id, tags)</h2>
    <p class="lede">Singletons inside their own OS bucket. Fixes Q1's fragmentation: a Debian-only baseline does not look like a singleton in a mixed Debian/RHEL fleet. Only peer groups with &gt;2 hosts are included (smaller groups have no baseline to compare against).</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q3">
