            <td class="num">0</td>
          </tr>
        
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q11">
    <h2>Q11 · Orphan exec_target OUTSIDE tmp-class directories</h2>
    <p class="lede">The implant pattern Q4 and Q9 miss entirely: the attacker drops the payload under a long-lived but unmanaged path (<code>/opt/</code>, <code>/var/lib/</code>, <code>/srv/</code>, <code>/usr/local/</code>) and wires persistence to it. The payload is not in <code>/tmp</code> so <code>interpreter_in_tmp</code> does not fire; the payload exists on disk so <code>exec_target_orphan</code> does not fire either. The only signal that catches it is <code>non_package_path</code> from the provenance resolver. LFA-sorted (hosts ascending): singletons are the highest-precision hits.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q11">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q11">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>exec_target</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th>module</th>
          <th>site_class</th>
          <th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th>
          <th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        
          <tr>
            <td><code>/usr/local/bin/sync</code></td>
            <td class="num">1</td>
            <td class="num">3</td>
            <td>cron</td>
            <td>cron.daily</td>
            <td>h5</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/cron.daily/sync</td>
            <td class="snippet">sync-cron-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
          <tr>
            <td><code>/opt/notthere/agent</code></td>
            <td class="num">1</td>
            <td class="num">1</td>
            <td>systemd</td>
            <td>systemd.unit</td>
            <td>h4</td>
            <td class="path">/etc/systemd/system/beacon.service</td>
            <td class="snippet">beacon-svc-norm</td>
          </tr>
        
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q12">
    <h2>Q12 · Campaign basename clusters</h2>
    <p class="lede">Same basename of <code>exec_target</code> (or <code>locus</code> when exec_target is empty) appearing in two or more modules across two or more hosts, where at least one arm carries a persistence-anomaly signal (<code>non_package_path</code> / <code>exec_target_orphan</code> / <code>interpreter_in_tmp</code>). Surfaces multi-arm campaigns whose individual arms each look like Q1 singletons in their own module (the v0.2.0 deploy-sync pattern); coincidental package baseline shared fleet-wide is excluded. Sorted ascending by host count.</p>
    <p class="hint">Expect FPs from vendor baselines shipping the same name in <code>systemd.unit</code> and <code>sysv.init</code> (nginx, redis-server, prometheus, cron). Triage from the top -- rare cross-module pairs are the interesting ones.</p>
    
    <p class="hint">No rows. Either the fleet contains no cross-module basename overlaps, or every overlap landed on a single host.</p>
    
  </section>


</main>

<script>// linpersist-report inline JavaScript.
//
// Vanilla, ~80 LOC. Three features:
//   1. Tab navigation: click a <button data-tab="..."> shows the
//      matching <section data-pane="...">.
//   2. Column sort: click <th> toggles asc/desc on the column. Uses
//      data-sort-type="num" for numeric columns, default lexicographic.
//   3. Live filter: <input class="search" data-target="#table-id">
//      filters rows by substring against the row's text content.
(function () {
  function $(sel, scope) { return (scope || document).querySelector(sel); }
  function $$(sel, scope) { return Array.from((scope || document).querySelectorAll(sel)); }

  // --- Tabs ---
  function activatePane(name) {
    $$('section.pane').forEach(function (p) {
      p.classList.toggle('active', p.dataset.pane === name);
    });
    $$('nav.tabs button').forEach(function (b) {
      b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.tab === name);
    });
    if (history.replaceState) {
      history.replaceState(null, '', '#' + name);
    }
  }
  $$('nav.tabs button').forEach(function (b) {
    b.addEventListener('click', function () { activatePane(b.dataset.tab); });
  });
  var initial = (location.hash || '#overview').slice(1);
  activatePane(initial);

  // --- Sortable tables ---
  function compare(a, b, type) {
    if (type === 'num') {
      var na = parseFloat(a), nb = parseFloat(b);
      if (isNaN(na)) na = -Infinity;
      if (isNaN(nb)) nb = -Infinity;
      return na - nb;
    }
    return a.localeCompare(b);
  }
  $$('table.sortable').forEach(function (table) {
    var ths = $$('th', table);
    ths.forEach(function (th, idx) {
      th.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var asc = !th.classList.contains('sort-asc');
        ths.forEach(function (x) { x.classList.remove('sort-asc', 'sort-desc'); });
        th.classList.add(asc ? 'sort-asc' : 'sort-desc');
        var type = th.dataset.sortType || '';
        var tbody = $('tbody', table);
        var rows = $$('tr', tbody);
        rows.sort(function (r1, r2) {
          var c1 = r1.children[idx] ? r1.children[idx].textContent.trim() : '';
          var c2 = r2.children[idx] ? r2.children[idx].textContent.trim() : '';
          var v = compare(c1, c2, type);
          return asc ? v : -v;
        });
        rows.forEach(function (r) { tbody.appendChild(r); });
      });
    });
  });

  // --- Live filters ---
  $$('input.search').forEach(function (inp) {
    inp.addEventListener('input', function () {
      var q = inp.value.trim().toLowerCase();
      var table = $(inp.dataset.target);
      if (!table) return;
      $$('tbody tr', table).forEach(function (r) {
        var text = r.textContent.toLowerCase();
        r.style.display = (q === '' || text.indexOf(q) !== -1) ? '' : 'none';
      });
    });
  });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
